# ItemAction_Hidapipe (ps2.asm:14573): on Motavia, "$13" and on the next
# button SXFID_Hidapipe waited out in place, then $FFFFCB0E = $FFFF --
# ProcessRandomBattle's counter then gains 2 a step on foot instead of 4
# -- and the item is used up. loc_6F1C clears it on the next way into a
# dungeon (a level under $10 into one of $10 up), and only then. Before
# build 73 the port played the sound and took the item but never set the
# flag, so it did nothing.
#
# A new game on Motavia near Shure, a Hidapipe given to Rolf (his fourth
# item). "The tones cover the sound of {char}'s steps." ($13) runs on
# with no button, the sound is waited out (some 470 ticks) and the menu
# closes by itself. Then the step up into Shure's door at 131,25.

start level 0 128 27
wait idle
give Hidapipe 0
expect hidapipe off
press c                      # ITEM, Rolf, the Hidapipe, USE
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press down
press down
press down
press c
wait idle
press c                      # USE
wait idle
expect script $0013
expect hidapipe on
shot 01_used
walk right 2
walk up 2                    # 130,26, then into the door
wait screen level
wait idle
expect level $17
expect hidapipe off
expect no-stderr not ported
